// Words for Word of the Day. Every word is 5 letters and comes with the KJV verse it appears in,
// plus one short line on why it matters. Add a word by copying a line.
window.BIBLE_WORDS = [
  { w: 'FAITH', ref: 'Hebrews 11:1', text: 'Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.', point: 'Faith is trusting God for what you can’t see yet, because of who he has already shown himself to be in Jesus.' },
  { w: 'GRACE', ref: 'Ephesians 2:8', text: 'For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God.', point: 'You can’t earn it and you can’t lose it by being imperfect. Grace is a gift Jesus paid for.' },
  { w: 'MOSES', ref: 'Exodus 3:4', text: 'God called unto him out of the midst of the bush, and said, Moses, Moses. And he said, Here am I.', point: 'God called Moses by name. He still knows yours.' },
  { w: 'JONAH', ref: 'Jonah 1:17', text: 'Now the LORD had prepared a great fish to swallow up Jonah. And Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights.', point: 'Jesus said Jonah’s three days pointed to his own death and resurrection (Matthew 12:40).' },
  { w: 'JESUS', ref: 'Matthew 1:21', text: 'And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins.', point: 'His name means “the LORD saves”, and that is exactly what he came to do.' },
  { w: 'MERCY', ref: 'Micah 6:8', text: 'And what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?', point: 'God has shown us mercy in Jesus, and he asks us to love showing it to others.' },
  { w: 'PEACE', ref: 'John 14:27', text: 'Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you.', point: 'The peace Jesus gives doesn’t depend on everything going well.' },
  { w: 'LIGHT', ref: 'John 8:12', text: 'I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.', point: 'Following Jesus doesn’t mean you’ll never face dark times. It means you won’t walk through them alone.' },
  { w: 'CROSS', ref: 'Luke 9:23', text: 'If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow me.', point: 'Jesus carried his cross for us. Following him is a daily choice, not a one-time event.' },
  { w: 'ANGEL', ref: 'Luke 2:10', text: 'And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people.', point: 'The good news of Jesus was announced to shepherds first. It’s for everyone.' },
  { w: 'BREAD', ref: 'John 6:35', text: 'I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.', point: 'Jesus satisfies a hunger nothing else can fill.' },
  { w: 'DAVID', ref: '1 Samuel 17:45', text: 'Then said David to the Philistine, Thou comest to me with a sword, and with a spear, and with a shield: but I come to thee in the name of the LORD of hosts.', point: 'David’s confidence wasn’t in himself. Jesus, the Son of David, won the biggest battle for us.' },
  { w: 'GLORY', ref: 'Luke 2:14', text: 'Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.', point: 'Heaven celebrated the night Jesus was born, because God had come to bring peace.' },
  { w: 'HEART', ref: 'Proverbs 3:5', text: 'Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.', point: 'God wants all of your trust, not just the parts you can’t handle yourself.' },
  { w: 'TRUTH', ref: 'John 14:6', text: 'Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.', point: 'Truth isn’t just an idea. Jesus said he is the truth.' },
  { w: 'WORLD', ref: 'John 3:16', text: 'For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.', point: '“Whosoever” includes you.' },
  { w: 'SAVED', ref: 'Acts 16:31', text: 'And they said, Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved, and thy house.', point: 'A jailer asked what he must do to be saved. The answer was simple: believe on Jesus.' },
  { w: 'ISAAC', ref: 'Genesis 22:2', text: 'And he said, Take now thy son, thine only son Isaac, whom thou lovest, and get thee into the land of Moriah; and offer him there for a burnt offering.', point: 'God provided a ram for Isaac. Centuries later he provided Jesus, the Lamb of God, for us.' },
  { w: 'SARAH', ref: 'Genesis 21:1', text: 'And the LORD visited Sarah as he had said, and the LORD did unto Sarah as he had spoken.', point: 'Sarah laughed at the promise, and God kept it anyway. He keeps his word.' },
  { w: 'AARON', ref: 'Exodus 17:12', text: 'But Moses’ hands were heavy; and they took a stone, and put it under him, and he sat thereon; and Aaron and Hur stayed up his hands.', point: 'Even Moses needed friends to hold him up. Church family matters.' },
  { w: 'PETER', ref: 'Matthew 16:18', text: 'And I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.', point: 'Jesus built his church on people like Peter: bold, flawed and forgiven.' },
  { w: 'EGYPT', ref: 'Matthew 2:15', text: 'And was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son.', point: 'Jesus relived Israel’s story, from Egypt onwards, and got right everything we get wrong.' },
  { w: 'JACOB', ref: 'Genesis 32:28', text: 'And he said, Thy name shall be called no more Jacob, but Israel: for as a prince hast thou power with God and with men, and hast prevailed.', point: 'God changed a schemer’s name and future. He can change yours too.' },
  { w: 'MANNA', ref: 'Exodus 16:31', text: 'And the house of Israel called the name thereof Manna: and it was like coriander seed, white; and the taste of it was like wafers made with honey.', point: 'God fed his people one day at a time. Jesus taught us to pray, “Give us this day our daily bread.”' },
  { w: 'STONE', ref: '1 Samuel 17:49', text: 'And David put his hand in his bag, and took thence a stone, and slang it, and smote the Philistine in his forehead.', point: 'One small stone in God’s hands was enough.' },
  { w: 'SWORD', ref: 'Ephesians 6:17', text: 'And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God.', point: 'Jesus fought temptation by quoting Scripture. The Word is a weapon worth knowing.' },
  { w: 'WATER', ref: 'John 4:14', text: 'But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst.', point: 'Jesus offered living water to a woman everyone else avoided.' },
  { w: 'RISEN', ref: 'Matthew 28:6', text: 'He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.', point: 'The empty tomb is the heart of the Christian faith. Jesus is alive.' },
  { w: 'ALTAR', ref: '1 Kings 18:30', text: 'And Elijah said unto all the people, Come near unto me. And all the people came near unto him. And he repaired the altar of the LORD that was broken down.', point: 'Before the fire fell, Elijah rebuilt what was broken. God restores.' },
  { w: 'CROWN', ref: 'James 1:12', text: 'Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.', point: 'Jesus wore a crown of thorns so we could receive a crown of life.' },
  { w: 'SHEEP', ref: 'John 10:11', text: 'I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.', point: 'A good shepherd doesn’t run when danger comes. Jesus gave his life for his sheep.' },
  { w: 'FLOOD', ref: 'Genesis 9:11', text: 'And I will establish my covenant with you; neither shall all flesh be cut off any more by the waters of a flood.', point: 'Every rainbow is a reminder that God keeps his promises.' },
  { w: 'BLOOD', ref: '1 John 1:7', text: 'But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.', point: 'Not some sin. All sin.' },
  { w: 'FRUIT', ref: 'Galatians 5:22', text: 'But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith.', point: 'Fruit grows when you stay connected to Jesus, the vine (John 15:5).' },
  { w: 'TRUST', ref: 'Psalm 56:3', text: 'What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.', point: 'Faith isn’t the absence of fear. It’s knowing who to run to when you’re afraid.' },
  { w: 'STAFF', ref: 'Psalm 23:4', text: 'Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.', point: 'Jesus called himself the good shepherd. He walks through the valley with you.' },
  { w: 'BIRTH', ref: 'Matthew 1:18', text: 'Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.', point: 'God didn’t send a message from far away. He came as a baby.' },
  { w: 'CHILD', ref: 'Isaiah 9:6', text: 'For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.', point: 'Isaiah wrote this about 700 years before Jesus was born.' },
  { w: 'HOUSE', ref: 'Joshua 24:15', text: 'But as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD.', point: 'Joshua decided for himself before anyone else did. Following God starts with your own choice.' },
  { w: 'PRIZE', ref: 'Philippians 3:14', text: 'I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.', point: 'Paul kept running because the prize was knowing Jesus.' },
  { w: 'YOUTH', ref: '1 Timothy 4:12', text: 'Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.', point: 'Being young doesn’t disqualify you. You can lead by example right now.' },
  { w: 'VOICE', ref: '1 Kings 19:12', text: 'And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.', point: 'God isn’t always in the loudest moment. Sometimes he whispers.' },
  { w: 'EARTH', ref: 'Genesis 1:1', text: 'In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.', point: 'John 1 says Jesus was there in the beginning, and all things were made by him.' },
  // ---------- More words (people) ----------
  { w: 'ABRAM', ref: 'Genesis 12:1', text: 'Now the LORD had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father’s house, unto a land that I will shew thee.', point: 'Abram stepped out without a map. Through his family, God would one day send Jesus to bless the whole world.' },
  { w: 'CALEB', ref: 'Numbers 14:24', text: 'But my servant Caleb, because he had another spirit with him, and hath followed me fully, him will I bring into the land whereinto he went; and his seed shall possess it.', point: 'Caleb followed God fully when the crowd was scared. Wholehearted beats half-hearted.' },
  { w: 'ENOCH', ref: 'Genesis 5:24', text: 'And Enoch walked with God: and he was not; for God took him.', point: 'Enoch’s whole life is summed up in three words: walked with God. In Jesus, you can walk with God too.' },
  { w: 'NAOMI', ref: 'Ruth 1:20', text: 'And she said unto them, Call me not Naomi, call me Mara: for the Almighty hath dealt very bitterly with me.', point: 'Naomi felt bitter, but God was quietly writing a happy ending. Her great-grandson’s line led to Jesus.' },
  { w: 'RAHAB', ref: 'Hebrews 11:31', text: 'By faith the harlot Rahab perished not with them that believed not, when she had received the spies with peace.', point: 'Rahab’s past didn’t stop God. She is named in the family line of Jesus (Matthew 1:5).' },
  { w: 'SIMON', ref: 'Luke 22:31', text: 'And the Lord said, Simon, Simon, behold, Satan hath desired to have you, that he may sift you as wheat:', point: 'Jesus warned Peter, then prayed for him. He knows your weak spots and prays for you too.' },
  { w: 'JAMES', ref: 'James 1:1', text: 'James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting.', point: 'James grew up in the same house as Jesus, yet he called himself Jesus’ servant.' },
  { w: 'JUDAH', ref: 'Genesis 49:10', text: 'The sceptre shall not depart from Judah, nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come;', point: 'Jesus is called the Lion of the tribe of Judah (Revelation 5:5).' },
  { w: 'JUDAS', ref: 'Luke 22:48', text: 'But Jesus said unto him, Judas, betrayest thou the Son of man with a kiss?', point: 'Even at the betrayal, Jesus spoke to Judas by name. He knew the cost and went to the cross anyway.' },
  { w: 'CYRUS', ref: 'Ezra 1:1', text: 'the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia,', point: 'God can move the heart of a king to bring his people home. Nobody is outside his reach.' },
  { w: 'HAMAN', ref: 'Esther 7:10', text: 'So they hanged Haman on the gallows that he had prepared for Mordecai.', point: 'Haman’s evil plan turned back on him. God protects his people, even when his name isn’t mentioned.' },
  { w: 'HEROD', ref: 'Matthew 2:13', text: 'for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him.', point: 'A powerful king tried to stop Jesus. He couldn’t. God’s plan to save us was never in danger.' },
  { w: 'JABEZ', ref: '1 Chronicles 4:10', text: 'And Jabez called on the God of Israel, saying, Oh that thou wouldest bless me indeed, and enlarge my coast, and that thine hand might be with me, and that thou wouldest keep me from evil, that it may not grieve me! And God granted him that which he requested.', point: 'Jabez’s name was linked with pain, but he prayed big and God answered. Your past is not your future.' },
  { w: 'JESSE', ref: 'Isaiah 11:1', text: 'And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots:', point: 'Jesse was David’s father. Isaiah promised that from his family tree would come the Branch: Jesus.' },
  { w: 'LYDIA', ref: 'Acts 16:14', text: 'And a certain woman named Lydia, a seller of purple, of the city of Thyatira, which worshipped God, heard us: whose heart the Lord opened, that she attended unto the things which were spoken of Paul.', point: 'A busy businesswoman by a riverside prayer meeting, and the Lord opened her heart to Jesus.' },
  { w: 'SILAS', ref: 'Acts 16:25', text: 'And at midnight Paul and Silas prayed, and sang praises unto God: and the prisoners heard them.', point: 'Beaten and locked up, they sang. Joy in Jesus doesn’t wait for good circumstances.' },
  { w: 'HAGAR', ref: 'Genesis 21:17', text: 'And God heard the voice of the lad; and the angel of God called to Hagar out of heaven, and said unto her, What aileth thee, Hagar? fear not; for God hath heard the voice of the lad where he is.', point: 'Alone in the desert, Hagar learned that God sees and hears the people everyone else overlooks.' },
  { w: 'ORPAH', ref: 'Ruth 1:14', text: 'And they lifted up their voice, and wept again: and Orpah kissed her mother in law; but Ruth clave unto her.', point: 'Orpah turned back; Ruth held on. Some choices shape everything that follows.' },
  { w: 'HOSEA', ref: 'Hosea 1:1', text: 'The word of the LORD that came unto Hosea, the son of Beeri,', point: 'Hosea’s life showed God’s love chasing an unfaithful people. Jesus is that love in person.' },
  { w: 'MICAH', ref: 'Micah 1:1', text: 'The word of the LORD that came to Micah the Morasthite', point: 'Micah named Bethlehem as the town where the coming ruler would be born (Micah 5:2).' },
  { w: 'TITUS', ref: 'Titus 1:4', text: 'To Titus, mine own son after the common faith:', point: 'Paul treated young Titus like a son in the faith. Everyone needs someone cheering them on.' },
  { w: 'RHODA', ref: 'Acts 12:13', text: 'And as Peter knocked at the door of the gate, a damsel came to hearken, named Rhoda.', point: 'Rhoda was so excited that God answered prayer, she forgot to open the door!' },
  { w: 'FELIX', ref: 'Acts 24:25', text: 'And as he reasoned of righteousness, temperance, and judgment to come, Felix trembled, and answered, Go thy way for this time; when I have a convenient season, I will call for thee.', point: 'Felix kept waiting for a “convenient” time to follow Jesus. Don’t put off the most important choice.' },
  { w: 'DEMAS', ref: '2 Timothy 4:10', text: 'For Demas hath forsaken me, having loved this present world,', point: 'Demas started well but drifted. Finishing with Jesus matters as much as starting.' },
  // ---------- Places ----------
  { w: 'BABEL', ref: 'Genesis 11:9', text: 'Therefore is the name of it called Babel; because the LORD did there confound the language of all the earth:', point: 'At Babel people tried to reach heaven by themselves. At the cross, heaven came down to us.' },
  { w: 'SINAI', ref: 'Exodus 19:20', text: 'And the LORD came down upon mount Sinai, on the top of the mount:', point: 'At Sinai God gave his law. Jesus kept it perfectly for everyone who couldn’t.' },
  { w: 'SODOM', ref: 'Genesis 19:24', text: 'Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the LORD out of heaven;', point: 'God takes sin seriously. That’s why the rescue Jesus offers is such good news.' },
  { w: 'JOPPA', ref: 'Jonah 1:3', text: 'But Jonah rose up to flee unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD, and went down to Joppa;', point: 'Running from God always goes “down”. Coming back to him is the way up.' },
  { w: 'HOREB', ref: '1 Kings 19:8', text: 'And he arose, and did eat and drink, and went in the strength of that meat forty days and forty nights unto Horeb the mount of God.', point: 'God fed a tired, discouraged Elijah before he spoke to him. He cares for your body and your heart.' },
  { w: 'NOBLE', ref: 'Acts 17:11', text: 'These were more noble than those in Thessalonica, in that they received the word with all readiness of mind, and searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so.', point: 'The Bereans checked everything against Scripture. Asking questions is part of real faith.' },
  // ---------- Things and creatures ----------
  { w: 'BRASS', ref: 'Numbers 21:9', text: 'And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put it upon a pole,', point: 'Jesus said that serpent on a pole pictured him being lifted up on the cross (John 3:14).' },
  { w: 'BRICK', ref: 'Exodus 5:7', text: 'Ye shall no more give the people straw to make brick, as heretofore:', point: 'Pharaoh made the work harder, but God was about to set his people free.' },
  { w: 'CHAFF', ref: 'Psalm 1:4', text: 'The ungodly are not so: but are like the chaff which the wind driveth away.', point: 'At harvest, chaff blows away in the breeze. A life rooted in God stays put.' },
  { w: 'DOVES', ref: 'Matthew 10:16', text: 'be ye therefore wise as serpents, and harmless as doves.', point: 'Jesus wants his followers smart and kind at the same time.' },
  { w: 'GOURD', ref: 'Jonah 4:6', text: 'And the LORD God prepared a gourd, and made it to come up over Jonah,', point: 'Jonah cared more about a plant than a city. God cares about people most of all.' },
  { w: 'SPEAR', ref: 'John 19:34', text: 'But one of the soldiers with a spear pierced his side, and forthwith came there out blood and water.', point: 'Jesus really died for us. That’s what makes his resurrection so amazing.' },
  { w: 'SWINE', ref: 'Luke 15:15', text: 'and he sent him into his fields to feed swine.', point: 'The lost son hit rock bottom feeding pigs. That’s where he remembered his father’s love.' },
  { w: 'HORSE', ref: 'Proverbs 21:31', text: 'The horse is prepared against the day of battle: but safety is of the LORD.', point: 'Prepare well, then trust God with the outcome.' },
  { w: 'EAGLE', ref: 'Isaiah 40:31', text: 'they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.', point: 'Eagles ride the wind instead of flapping hard. Waiting on God gives strength you don’t have to make yourself.' },
  { w: 'FROGS', ref: 'Exodus 8:2', text: 'And if thou refuse to let them go, behold, I will smite all thy borders with frogs:', point: 'Frogs in the beds and in the ovens! God is stronger than any power that holds people captive.' },
  { w: 'QUAIL', ref: 'Exodus 16:13', text: 'And it came to pass, that at even the quails came up, and covered the camp:', point: 'God answered grumbling with dinner. He is more generous than we deserve.' },
  { w: 'RAVEN', ref: '1 Kings 17:6', text: 'And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening; and he drank of the brook.', point: 'God used birds as a delivery service. He can provide in ways you’d never expect.' },
  { w: 'CAMEL', ref: 'Matthew 19:24', text: 'And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.', point: 'Nobody can squeeze into heaven by effort. Jesus said, “with God all things are possible.”' },
  { w: 'WHALE', ref: 'Matthew 12:40', text: 'For as Jonas was three days and three nights in the whale’s belly; so shall the Son of man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.', point: 'Jesus used Jonah’s story to point to his own death and resurrection.' },
  { w: 'TOWEL', ref: 'John 13:4', text: 'He riseth from supper, and laid aside his garments; and took a towel, and girded himself.', point: 'The King of heaven picked up a towel and washed feet. Greatness looks like serving.' },
  { w: 'NAILS', ref: 'John 20:25', text: 'Except I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and thrust my hand into his side, I will not believe.', point: 'Jesus showed doubting Thomas his scars. He welcomes honest questions.' },
  { w: 'COALS', ref: 'John 21:9', text: 'As soon then as they were come to land, they saw a fire of coals there, and fish laid thereon, and bread.', point: 'The risen Jesus cooked breakfast for his tired friends. He meets you where you are.' },
  { w: 'MYRRH', ref: 'Matthew 2:11', text: 'and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.', point: 'Wise men travelled a long way to worship a child. Jesus is worth the journey.' },
  { w: 'LAMPS', ref: 'Matthew 25:1', text: 'Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.', point: 'Jesus told this story so we’d stay ready for his return.' },
  { w: 'PEARL', ref: 'Matthew 13:46', text: 'Who, when he had found one pearl of great price, went and sold all that he had, and bought it.', point: 'Knowing Jesus is worth more than everything else put together.' },
  { w: 'GLASS', ref: '1 Corinthians 13:12', text: 'For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face:', point: 'We don’t have all the answers now, but one day we’ll see Jesus face to face.' },
  { w: 'SHOES', ref: 'Luke 15:22', text: 'Bring forth the best robe, and put it on him; and put a ring on his hand, and shoes on his feet:', point: 'Servants went barefoot; sons wore shoes. The father welcomed his boy back as a son, not a servant.' },
  { w: 'HUSKS', ref: 'Luke 15:16', text: 'And he would fain have filled his belly with the husks that the swine did eat: and no man gave unto him.', point: 'The world’s “food” never satisfies for long. Jesus is the bread of life.' },
  { w: 'SKIRT', ref: '1 Samuel 24:4', text: 'Then David arose, and cut off the skirt of Saul’s robe privily.', point: 'David could have taken revenge in that cave, but he spared Saul. Mercy is stronger than payback.' },
  { w: 'FOXES', ref: 'Judges 15:4', text: 'And Samson went and caught three hundred foxes,', point: 'Samson was strong but often reckless. Jesus is the deliverer who never misused his power.' },
  { w: 'ARROW', ref: 'Psalm 91:5', text: 'Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; nor for the arrow that flieth by day;', point: 'Day or night, God is your shelter.' },
  { w: 'SNARE', ref: 'Psalm 91:3', text: 'Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, and from the noisome pestilence.', point: 'Like a bird slipping free of a trap, God can rescue you from what has you caught.' },
  // ---------- Nature and creation ----------
  { w: 'CEDAR', ref: 'Psalm 92:12', text: 'The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.', point: 'Cedars grow tall and strong slowly. Growing in Jesus takes time, and that’s fine.' },
  { w: 'CLOUD', ref: 'Exodus 13:21', text: 'And the LORD went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night.', point: 'God led his people every step. He still guides those who follow him.' },
  { w: 'FIELD', ref: 'John 4:35', text: 'Lift up your eyes, and look on the fields; for they are white already to harvest.', point: 'Like ripe crops before the rains, people all around are ready to hear about Jesus.' },
  { w: 'GREEN', ref: 'Psalm 23:2', text: 'He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.', point: 'The good shepherd knows when you need rest.' },
  { w: 'GRASS', ref: 'Isaiah 40:8', text: 'The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our God shall stand for ever.', point: 'Trends fade by the next rainy season. God’s word lasts for ever.' },
  { w: 'HILLS', ref: 'Psalm 121:1', text: 'I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help.', point: 'The next verse answers it: “My help cometh from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.”' },
  { w: 'NIGHT', ref: 'Psalm 30:5', text: 'weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.', point: 'Sad nights don’t last for ever. Easter morning proves it.' },
  { w: 'OLIVE', ref: 'Psalm 52:8', text: 'But I am like a green olive tree in the house of God: I trust in the mercy of God for ever and ever.', point: 'Olive trees can live for hundreds of years. Trust in God keeps you green.' },
  { w: 'RIVER', ref: 'Psalm 46:4', text: 'There is a river, the streams whereof shall make glad the city of God,', point: 'In the middle of chaos, God’s presence is like a river of joy.' },
  { w: 'STARS', ref: 'Genesis 15:5', text: 'Look now toward heaven, and tell the stars, if thou be able to number them:', point: 'God told Abram to count the stars. Everyone who trusts in Jesus is part of that huge family.' },
  { w: 'STORM', ref: 'Psalm 107:29', text: 'He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.', point: 'Jesus did exactly this on Galilee. The storm obeys him.' },
  { w: 'HAVEN', ref: 'Psalm 107:30', text: 'Then are they glad because they be quiet; so he bringeth them unto their desired haven.', point: 'God doesn’t just calm the storm; he brings you home.' },
  { w: 'WAVES', ref: 'Matthew 8:24', text: 'And, behold, there arose a great tempest in the sea, insomuch that the ship was covered with the waves: but he was asleep.', point: 'Jesus could sleep in the storm because he was never out of control.' },
  { w: 'WINDS', ref: 'Matthew 8:27', text: 'What manner of man is this, that even the winds and the sea obey him!', point: 'Only God commands the weather. The disciples were starting to see who Jesus really is.' },
  { w: 'SHORE', ref: 'John 21:4', text: 'But when the morning was now come, Jesus stood on the shore: but the disciples knew not that it was Jesus.', point: 'After a night of failure, Jesus was waiting on the shore.' },
  { w: 'WHEAT', ref: 'John 12:24', text: 'Verily, verily, I say unto you, Except a corn of wheat fall into the ground and die, it abideth alone: but if it die, it bringeth forth much fruit.', point: 'Jesus was talking about his own death, which brings life to millions.' },
  { w: 'PLANT', ref: '1 Corinthians 3:6', text: 'I have planted, Apollos watered; but God gave the increase.', point: 'You plant and water; God makes it grow. Every role in the team matters.' },
  { w: 'SHADE', ref: 'Psalm 121:5', text: 'The LORD is thy keeper: the LORD is thy shade upon thy right hand.', point: 'Like a big tree in the midday heat, God is cover and rest.' },
  { w: 'SOWER', ref: 'Matthew 13:3', text: 'Behold, a sower went forth to sow;', point: 'Jesus’ story asks: what kind of soil is your heart?' },
  { w: 'FLOCK', ref: 'Luke 12:32', text: 'Fear not, little flock; for it is your Father’s good pleasure to give you the kingdom.', point: 'God isn’t reluctant to bless you. It makes him happy to give.' },
  { w: 'GOATS', ref: 'Matthew 25:32', text: 'And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats:', point: 'Jesus said how we treat people in need shows whose we are.' },
  // ---------- Big ideas ----------
  { w: 'ABIDE', ref: 'John 15:4', text: 'Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, except it abide in the vine; no more can ye, except ye abide in me.', point: 'A branch doesn’t strain to grow fruit; it stays connected. Stay close to Jesus.' },
  { w: 'BLESS', ref: 'Numbers 6:24', text: 'The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:', point: 'God’s first word over his people was blessing. That’s his heart toward you.' },
  { w: 'BOAST', ref: 'Ephesians 2:9', text: 'Not of works, lest any man should boast.', point: 'Nobody gets to brag about earning heaven. It’s all a gift from Jesus.' },
  { w: 'CLEAN', ref: 'Psalm 51:10', text: 'Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.', point: 'David prayed this after a terrible failure. Jesus makes fresh starts possible.' },
  { w: 'COUNT', ref: 'James 1:2', text: 'My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations;', point: 'Hard times can grow your faith. Joy isn’t pretending; it’s trusting God is at work.' },
  { w: 'DEATH', ref: 'John 5:24', text: 'Verily, verily, I say unto you, He that heareth my word, and believeth on him that sent me, hath everlasting life, and shall not come into condemnation; but is passed from death unto life.', point: 'Believe on Jesus and you have already crossed from death to life.' },
  { w: 'WAGES', ref: 'Romans 6:23', text: 'For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.', point: 'Wages are earned. Gifts are free. Jesus offers the gift.' },
  { w: 'DWELL', ref: 'Psalm 23:6', text: 'Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.', point: 'God’s goodness doesn’t just wait for you; it follows you.' },
  { w: 'FAINT', ref: 'Isaiah 40:29', text: 'He giveth power to the faint; and to them that have no might he increaseth strength.', point: 'Running on empty? God gives strength to the tired, not just the strong.' },
  { w: 'FLESH', ref: 'John 1:14', text: 'And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.', point: 'God became a real human being. Jesus knows life from the inside.' },
  { w: 'GATES', ref: 'Psalm 24:7', text: 'Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and be ye lift up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.', point: 'Open the door for the King of glory. Jesus is ready to come in.' },
  { w: 'GIVEN', ref: 'Luke 6:38', text: 'Give, and it shall be given unto you; good measure, pressed down, and shaken together, and running over, shall men give into your bosom.', point: 'Like a market seller who adds a little extra, God gives back generously.' },
  { w: 'GREAT', ref: 'Lamentations 3:23', text: 'They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.', point: 'Every sunrise is a fresh supply of God’s mercy.' },
  { w: 'GUIDE', ref: 'John 16:13', text: 'Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth:', point: 'Jesus didn’t leave us alone. The Holy Spirit guides us.' },
  { w: 'HANDS', ref: 'Luke 23:46', text: 'Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit:', point: 'Jesus trusted his Father to the very end. Your life is safe in the same hands.' },
  { w: 'IDOLS', ref: '1 John 5:21', text: 'Little children, keep yourselves from idols. Amen.', point: 'An idol is anything we trust more than God: phones, fame, money. Keep Jesus first.' },
  { w: 'JUDGE', ref: 'Matthew 7:1', text: 'Judge not, that ye be not judged.', point: 'Jesus calls us to look at our own hearts before pointing fingers.' },
  { w: 'KINGS', ref: 'Revelation 19:16', text: 'And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.', point: 'Every ruler in history answers to Jesus.' },
  { w: 'LEARN', ref: 'Matthew 11:29', text: 'Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.', point: 'Jesus is a gentle teacher. Learning from him brings rest, not stress.' },
  { w: 'MIGHT', ref: 'Zechariah 4:6', text: 'Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.', point: 'God’s work isn’t powered by muscle or money but by his Spirit.' },
  { w: 'MONEY', ref: '1 Timothy 6:10', text: 'For the love of money is the root of all evil:', point: 'Money isn’t evil; loving it is. Jesus is the treasure that lasts.' },
  { w: 'MOUTH', ref: 'Psalm 19:14', text: 'Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.', point: 'A great prayer before you post, text or speak.' },
  { w: 'PROUD', ref: 'James 4:6', text: 'God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.', point: 'Pride pushes God away; humility opens the door to his grace.' },
  { w: 'PSALM', ref: 'Colossians 3:16', text: 'teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to the Lord.', point: 'Singing together at choir practice or youth fellowship is one way God’s word sinks in deep.' },
  { w: 'QUEEN', ref: '1 Kings 10:1', text: 'And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the name of the LORD, she came to prove him with hard questions.', point: 'Jesus said someone “greater than Solomon” had come: himself (Matthew 12:42).' },
  { w: 'REIGN', ref: 'Revelation 11:15', text: 'The kingdoms of this world are become the kingdoms of our Lord, and of his Christ; and he shall reign for ever and ever.', point: 'History is heading somewhere: to Jesus on the throne.' },
  { w: 'SATAN', ref: 'Romans 16:20', text: 'And the God of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.', point: 'The enemy is real but already defeated by Jesus at the cross.' },
  { w: 'SERVE', ref: 'Matthew 6:24', text: 'Ye cannot serve God and mammon.', point: 'You can’t have two bosses. Jesus asks to be first.' },
  { w: 'SHAME', ref: 'Hebrews 12:2', text: 'Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.', point: 'Jesus carried our shame so we don’t have to.' },
  { w: 'SHINE', ref: 'Matthew 5:16', text: 'Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.', point: 'Your kindness can point people to God.' },
  { w: 'SLEEP', ref: 'Psalm 121:4', text: 'Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.', point: 'You can sleep in peace because God never does.' },
  { w: 'SLING', ref: '1 Samuel 17:50', text: 'So David prevailed over the Philistine with a sling and with a stone,', point: 'An ordinary sling plus faith in God beat a giant.' },
  { w: 'SPEAK', ref: '1 Samuel 3:10', text: 'Speak; for thy servant heareth.', point: 'Young Samuel learned to listen for God. You’re never too young to hear him.' },
  { w: 'STAND', ref: 'Ephesians 6:13', text: 'Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand.', point: 'Sometimes victory simply means still standing, held up by God.' },
  { w: 'TABLE', ref: 'Psalm 23:5', text: 'Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.', point: 'God throws a feast for you even when trouble is near.' },
  { w: 'TEACH', ref: 'Psalm 90:12', text: 'So teach us to number our days, that we may apply our hearts unto wisdom.', point: 'Life is short. Spend it on what lasts.' },
  { w: 'TEARS', ref: 'Revelation 21:4', text: 'And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.', point: 'Because Jesus rose, a world with no more tears is coming.' },
  { w: 'THIEF', ref: 'John 10:10', text: 'The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.', point: 'Jesus came to give life, full and overflowing.' },
  { w: 'THORN', ref: '2 Corinthians 12:7', text: 'there was given to me a thorn in the flesh, the messenger of Satan to buffet me,', point: 'God told Paul, “My grace is sufficient for thee.” Weakness is where his strength shows.' },
  { w: 'THREE', ref: 'Matthew 18:20', text: 'For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.', point: 'Even a tiny prayer group under a tree has Jesus in the middle.' },
  { w: 'UNITY', ref: 'Psalm 133:1', text: 'Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!', point: 'Getting along isn’t boring; God calls it good and pleasant.' },
  { w: 'WALLS', ref: 'Hebrews 11:30', text: 'By faith the walls of Jericho fell down, after they were compassed about seven days.', point: 'They just walked and trusted. God did the rest.' },
  { w: 'WATCH', ref: 'Matthew 26:41', text: 'Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.', point: 'Jesus knows we’re weak. Prayer is how we stay alert.' },
  { w: 'WINGS', ref: 'Psalm 91:4', text: 'He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust:', point: 'Like a hen covering her chicks in the compound when the storm comes, God shelters you.' },
  { w: 'WOMAN', ref: 'Galatians 4:4', text: 'But when the fulness of the time was come, God sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law,', point: 'Right on God’s schedule, Jesus was born.' },
  { w: 'WORKS', ref: 'Ephesians 2:10', text: 'For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them.', point: 'Good works don’t save you, but you were saved to do them.' },
  { w: 'WRATH', ref: 'Proverbs 15:1', text: 'A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.', point: 'In a heated group chat, a gentle reply can calm everything down.' },
  { w: 'ALIVE', ref: 'Luke 15:24', text: 'For this my son was dead, and is alive again; he was lost, and is found.', point: 'Heaven throws a party when one person comes home to God.' },
  { w: 'ANGRY', ref: 'Ephesians 4:26', text: 'Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:', point: 'Feelings aren’t sin. Holding onto them is the danger. Settle it before bedtime.' },
  { w: 'KNOCK', ref: 'Revelation 3:20', text: 'Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.', point: 'Jesus doesn’t force his way in. He knocks and waits.' },
  { w: 'AWAKE', ref: 'Ephesians 5:14', text: 'Awake thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ shall give thee light.', point: 'Jesus wakes up sleepy hearts.' },
  { w: 'ARISE', ref: 'Isaiah 60:1', text: 'Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the LORD is risen upon thee.', point: 'You don’t make the light; you reflect it. Jesus is the light that has come.' },
  { w: 'BLIND', ref: 'John 9:25', text: 'one thing I know, that, whereas I was blind, now I see.', point: 'You don’t need every answer to tell people what Jesus did for you.' },
  { w: 'BONES', ref: 'Ezekiel 37:4', text: 'Again he said unto me, Prophesy upon these bones, and say unto them, O ye dry bones, hear the word of the LORD.', point: 'God can bring life to what looks completely dead.' },
  { w: 'BRIDE', ref: 'Revelation 21:2', text: 'And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.', point: 'The Bible ends with a wedding: Jesus and his people together for ever.' },
  { w: 'BUILD', ref: 'Psalm 127:1', text: 'Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it:', point: 'Plans work best when God is the builder.' },
  { w: 'DAILY', ref: 'Acts 2:47', text: 'And the Lord added to the church daily such as should be saved.', point: 'The early church grew every day as people met Jesus.' },
  { w: 'DREAM', ref: 'Joel 2:28', text: 'and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, your old men shall dream dreams, your young men shall see visions:', point: 'God pours out his Spirit on young and old alike.' },
  { w: 'ENTER', ref: 'Matthew 7:13', text: 'Enter ye in at the strait gate:', point: 'The narrow way is Jesus himself. It’s worth it.' },
  { w: 'EXALT', ref: 'Psalm 34:3', text: 'O magnify the LORD with me, and let us exalt his name together.', point: 'Worship is better together.' },
  { w: 'FIRST', ref: 'Matthew 6:33', text: 'But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.', point: 'Put God first and trust him with the rest.' },
  { w: 'FOUND', ref: 'Luke 15:6', text: 'Rejoice with me; for I have found my sheep which was lost.', point: 'Jesus is the shepherd who goes looking for you.' },
  { w: 'GIFTS', ref: 'Matthew 7:11', text: 'If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?', point: 'If a good mum or dad gives good things, imagine how much more God does.' },
  { w: 'GRAVE', ref: '1 Corinthians 15:55', text: 'O death, where is thy sting? O grave, where is thy victory?', point: 'Because Jesus rose, death has lost its sting.' },
  { w: 'HAPPY', ref: 'Psalm 144:15', text: 'Happy is that people, that is in such a case: yea, happy is that people, whose God is the LORD.', point: 'Real happiness is knowing God.' },
  { w: 'HONEY', ref: 'Psalm 119:103', text: 'How sweet are thy words unto my taste! yea, sweeter than honey to my mouth!', point: 'God’s word can be a treat, not a chore.' },
  { w: 'HOSTS', ref: 'Isaiah 6:3', text: 'Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.', point: 'Angels can’t stop saying it: God is holy. Jesus makes it possible to come near.' },
  { w: 'IMAGE', ref: 'Genesis 1:27', text: 'So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.', point: 'Every person you meet carries God’s image. That’s why everyone matters.' },
  { w: 'LEAST', ref: 'Matthew 25:40', text: 'Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.', point: 'Helping someone in need is serving Jesus himself.' },
  { w: 'LEPER', ref: 'Matthew 8:2', text: 'And, behold, there came a leper and worshipped him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.', point: 'Jesus touched the untouchable and said, “I will; be thou clean.”' },
  { w: 'LIONS', ref: 'Daniel 6:22', text: 'My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions’ mouths, that they have not hurt me:', point: 'Daniel kept praying when it was dangerous. God kept him safe.' },
  { w: 'LOVED', ref: '1 John 4:19', text: 'We love him, because he first loved us.', point: 'God made the first move. Our love is just a response to his.' },
  { w: 'ORDER', ref: '1 Corinthians 14:40', text: 'Let all things be done decently and in order.', point: 'God is a God of peace, not chaos.' },
  { w: 'POWER', ref: 'Acts 1:8', text: 'But ye shall receive power, after that the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth.', point: 'The Spirit gives ordinary people power to tell others about Jesus.' },
  { w: 'PRIDE', ref: 'Proverbs 16:18', text: 'Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.', point: 'Pride trips you up. Humility keeps you steady.' },
  { w: 'READY', ref: '1 Peter 3:15', text: 'be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you with meekness and fear:', point: 'Be ready to explain why you follow Jesus, kindly.' },
  { w: 'ROYAL', ref: '1 Peter 2:9', text: 'But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people;', point: 'In Jesus, you are royalty. Live like it.' },
  { w: 'SEVEN', ref: 'Matthew 18:22', text: 'Jesus saith unto him, I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven.', point: 'Stop counting. Forgive like you have been forgiven.' },
  { w: 'SIGHT', ref: '2 Corinthians 5:7', text: '(For we walk by faith, not by sight:)', point: 'You don’t always see the path, but you can trust the one leading.' },
  { w: 'STEPS', ref: 'Psalm 37:23', text: 'The steps of a good man are ordered by the LORD: and he delighteth in his way.', point: 'God cares about each step, not just the destination.' },
  { w: 'SWIFT', ref: 'Ecclesiastes 9:11', text: 'the race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong,', point: 'Life doesn’t always go to the fastest. God is in charge of outcomes.' },
  { w: 'THANK', ref: '1 Thessalonians 5:18', text: 'In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.', point: 'Not thanks FOR everything, but IN everything. There’s always something.' },
  { w: 'TOWER', ref: 'Proverbs 18:10', text: 'The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.', point: 'When trouble comes, run to God.' },
  { w: 'WEARY', ref: 'Galatians 6:9', text: 'And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.', point: 'Doing good can feel unrewarded. Keep going; harvest is coming.' },
  { w: 'WHITE', ref: 'Isaiah 1:18', text: 'Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.', point: 'No stain is too deep for Jesus to wash away.' },
  { w: 'WIDOW', ref: 'Mark 12:42', text: 'And there came a certain poor widow, and she threw in two mites, which make a farthing.', point: 'Jesus said her tiny gift was the biggest, because she gave everything.' },
  { w: 'YEARS', ref: '2 Peter 3:8', text: 'one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.', point: 'God isn’t slow. He sees time differently and is patient with us.' },
  { w: 'AGAIN', ref: 'John 3:3', text: 'Jesus answered and said unto him, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God.', point: 'Jesus offers a whole new start, not just a better version of the old one.' },
  { w: 'ALPHA', ref: 'Revelation 22:13', text: 'I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end, the first and the last.', point: 'Alpha is the first Greek letter. Jesus was there before everything began.' },
  { w: 'OMEGA', ref: 'Revelation 1:8', text: 'I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, which is, and which was, and which is to come, the Almighty.', point: 'Omega is the last Greek letter. Jesus will have the final word.' },
  { w: 'ASHES', ref: 'Isaiah 61:3', text: 'to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness;', point: 'Jesus read from this part of Isaiah and said it was about him (Luke 4:21).' },
  { w: 'CHEER', ref: 'John 16:33', text: 'In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.', point: 'Trouble is real. So is Jesus’ victory.' },
  { w: 'DEVIL', ref: 'James 4:7', text: 'Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.', point: 'Stay close to God and the enemy has to run.' },
  { w: 'DOUBT', ref: 'Matthew 14:31', text: 'O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?', point: 'When Peter sank, Jesus reached out immediately. Doubt doesn’t make him let go.' },
  { w: 'FORTY', ref: 'Matthew 4:2', text: 'And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was afterward an hungred.', point: 'Hungry and alone, Jesus still beat temptation with God’s word.' },
  { w: 'LAUGH', ref: 'Genesis 21:6', text: 'And Sarah said, God hath made me to laugh, so that all that hear will laugh with me.', point: 'Isaac’s name means laughter. God can turn doubt into joy.' },
  { w: 'DANCE', ref: 'Ecclesiastes 3:4', text: 'A time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;', point: 'God made room in life for tears and for celebration.' },
  { w: 'LEAVE', ref: 'Hebrews 13:5', text: 'for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.', point: 'Friends move away, but Jesus never will.' },
  { w: 'MOURN', ref: 'Matthew 5:4', text: 'Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.', point: 'Jesus doesn’t rush your grief. He promises comfort.' },
  { w: 'QUICK', ref: 'Hebrews 4:12', text: 'For the word of God is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword,', point: '“Quick” here means alive. God’s word is living.' },
  { w: 'QUIET', ref: '1 Thessalonians 4:11', text: 'And that ye study to be quiet, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands, as we commanded you;', point: 'A quiet, hardworking life can say a lot about Jesus.' },
  { w: 'SHOUT', ref: 'Psalm 47:1', text: 'O clap your hands, all ye people; shout unto God with the voice of triumph.', point: 'Worship can be loud!' },
  { w: 'SOBER', ref: '1 Peter 5:8', text: 'Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:', point: 'Stay alert. Jesus, the Lion of Judah, is stronger.' },
  { w: 'TASTE', ref: 'Psalm 34:8', text: 'O taste and see that the LORD is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.', point: 'Like grandma’s cooking, you have to try it yourself. Taste and see.' },
  { w: 'TIMES', ref: 'Psalm 34:1', text: 'I will bless the LORD at all times: his praise shall continually be in my mouth.', point: 'All times means good days and hard ones.' },
  { w: 'HEIRS', ref: 'Romans 8:17', text: 'And if children, then heirs; heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ;', point: 'In Jesus you’re not a guest in God’s family; you’re an heir.' },
  { w: 'NOISE', ref: 'Psalm 100:1', text: 'Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all ye lands.', point: 'You don’t need a perfect voice to praise God. Joyful noise counts.' },
  { w: 'KNOWN', ref: 'Psalm 139:1', text: 'O LORD, thou hast searched me, and known me.', point: 'God knows everything about you and still loves you.' },
  { w: 'WORDS', ref: 'Proverbs 16:24', text: 'Pleasant words are as an honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.', point: 'Kind words are like medicine. Use them generously.' },
  { w: 'STILL', ref: 'Psalm 46:10', text: 'Be still, and know that I am God:', point: 'Put the phone down sometimes. Stillness helps you notice God.' },
  { w: 'STONY', ref: 'Ezekiel 36:26', text: 'A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.', point: 'God swaps hard hearts for soft ones. That’s what Jesus does in us.' },
  { w: 'TITHE', ref: 'Malachi 3:10', text: 'Bring ye all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in mine house,', point: 'Giving back to God shows you trust him to provide.' },
  { w: 'FIGHT', ref: '2 Timothy 4:7', text: 'I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith:', point: 'Paul finished strong. With Jesus, you can too.' },
  { w: 'SHORT', ref: 'Romans 3:23', text: 'For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;', point: 'Everyone falls short. Everyone can be forgiven through Jesus.' },
  { w: 'SWEET', ref: '2 Corinthians 2:15', text: 'For we are unto God a sweet savour of Christ,', point: 'Your life can carry the fragrance of Jesus wherever you go.' },
  { w: 'RIGHT', ref: 'Ephesians 6:1', text: 'Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right.', point: 'Honouring parents pleases God. Jesus did it too (Luke 2:51).' },
  { w: 'THINK', ref: 'Philippians 4:8', text: 'Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.', point: 'What you think about shapes who you become.' },
  { w: 'ABOVE', ref: 'Colossians 3:2', text: 'Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.', point: 'Keep your eyes on Jesus, not just the latest thing.' },
  { w: 'PROVE', ref: '1 Thessalonians 5:21', text: 'Prove all things; hold fast that which is good.', point: 'Test what you hear. Hold on to what’s true.' },
  { w: 'STUDY', ref: '2 Timothy 2:15', text: 'Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.', point: 'Getting to know the Bible is worth the effort, like studying for the exam that matters most.' },
  { w: 'DOERS', ref: 'James 1:22', text: 'But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.', point: 'Listening is good. Doing is better.' },
  { w: 'SLACK', ref: '2 Peter 3:9', text: 'The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.', point: 'God’s waiting is patience. He wants everyone to come home.' },
  { w: 'SLAIN', ref: 'Revelation 5:12', text: 'Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.', point: 'All of heaven praises Jesus, the Lamb who gave his life.' },
  { w: 'PRICE', ref: '1 Corinthians 6:20', text: 'For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God’s.', point: 'Jesus paid the highest price for you. You are that valuable.' },
  { w: 'PLACE', ref: 'John 14:2', text: 'In my Father’s house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.', point: 'Jesus is getting a place ready for you.' },
  { w: 'ABODE', ref: 'John 14:23', text: 'If a man love me, he will keep my words: and my Father will love him, and we will come unto him, and make our abode with him.', point: 'God doesn’t just visit; he moves in.' },
  { w: 'TRAIN', ref: 'Proverbs 22:6', text: 'Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.', point: 'What you learn about God young can last a lifetime.' },
  { w: 'SWEEP', ref: 'Luke 15:8', text: 'Either what woman having ten pieces of silver, if she lose one piece, doth not light a candle, and sweep the house, and seek diligently till she find it?', point: 'Like Zawadi turning the house upside down for one lost coin, God searches for each person.' },
  { w: 'MERRY', ref: 'Luke 15:23', text: 'And bring hither the fatted calf, and kill it; and let us eat, and be merry:', point: 'The father didn’t lecture; he threw a party. That’s how God welcomes you home.' },
  { w: 'ELDER', ref: 'Luke 15:25', text: 'Now his elder son was in the field:', point: 'The older brother stayed home but missed the father’s heart. Grace is for both brothers.' },
  { w: 'CHIEF', ref: 'Luke 19:2', text: 'And, behold, there was a man named Zacchaeus, which was the chief among the publicans, and he was rich.', point: 'The most unpopular man in town got a visit from Jesus.' },
  { w: 'CLIMB', ref: 'Luke 19:4', text: 'And he ran before, and climbed up into a sycomore tree to see him: for he was to pass that way.', point: 'Zacchaeus went out of his way to see Jesus, and Jesus stopped for him.' },
  { w: 'TOUCH', ref: 'Mark 5:28', text: 'For she said, If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole.', point: 'In a pushing crowd, Jesus noticed one desperate touch.' },
  { w: 'WHOLE', ref: 'Mark 5:34', text: 'And he said unto her, Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, and be whole of thy plague.', point: 'Jesus didn’t just heal her body; he called her “daughter”.' },
  { w: 'TWAIN', ref: 'Matthew 5:41', text: 'And whosoever shall compel thee to go a mile, go with him twain.', point: 'Go the extra mile, like Jesus went all the way for us.' },
  { w: 'CHEEK', ref: 'Matthew 5:39', text: 'but whosoever shall smite thee on thy right cheek, turn to him the other also.', point: 'Jesus calls us to break the cycle of revenge.' },
  { w: 'DEBTS', ref: 'Matthew 6:12', text: 'And forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors.', point: 'Forgiven people forgive people.' },
  { w: 'LOOSE', ref: 'John 11:44', text: 'Jesus saith unto them, Loose him, and let him go.', point: 'Jesus raised Lazarus, then had his friends help unwrap him. Freedom is a team effort.' },
  { w: 'SWEAT', ref: 'Luke 22:44', text: 'And being in an agony he prayed more earnestly: and his sweat was as it were great drops of blood falling down to the ground.', point: 'Jesus felt the full weight of what he was about to do, and chose it anyway.' },
  { w: 'THIRD', ref: '1 Corinthians 15:4', text: 'And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures:', point: 'The heart of the good news: Jesus died, was buried, and rose.' },
  { w: 'SOUND', ref: 'Acts 2:2', text: 'And suddenly there came a sound from heaven as of a rushing mighty wind, and it filled all the house where they were sitting.', point: 'At Pentecost the Holy Spirit came, just as Jesus had promised.' },
  { w: 'FIERY', ref: 'Daniel 3:17', text: 'If it be so, our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace, and he will deliver us out of thine hand, O king.', point: 'In the fire, a fourth man walked with them. God is with you in the heat.' },
  { w: 'GLEAN', ref: 'Ruth 2:2', text: 'Let me now go to the field, and glean ears of corn after him in whose sight I shall find grace.', point: 'Ruth worked hard at harvest, and found grace. Boaz’s kindness pictures Jesus our redeemer.' },
  { w: 'NAKED', ref: 'Job 1:21', text: 'Naked came I out of my mother’s womb, and naked shall I return thither: the LORD gave, and the LORD hath taken away; blessed be the name of the LORD.', point: 'Job lost everything and still worshipped. God was not finished with his story.' },
  { w: 'EARLY', ref: 'Psalm 63:1', text: 'O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee:', point: 'Start the day with God, even before the bus ride.' },
  { w: 'HEARD', ref: 'Psalm 34:6', text: 'This poor man cried, and the LORD heard him, and saved him out of all his troubles.', point: 'You don’t need fancy words. God hears a simple cry.' },
  { w: 'ENEMY', ref: 'Proverbs 25:21', text: 'If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink:', point: 'Kindness to enemies is how Jesus treated us.' },
  { w: 'GIVER', ref: '2 Corinthians 9:7', text: 'Every man according as he purposeth in his heart, so let him give; not grudgingly, or of necessity: for God loveth a cheerful giver.', point: 'Give with a smile. God gave his Son gladly.' },
  { w: 'SMALL', ref: 'Zechariah 4:10', text: 'For who hath despised the day of small things?', point: 'Small beginnings matter to God.' },
  { w: 'HAIRS', ref: 'Matthew 10:30', text: 'But the very hairs of your head are all numbered.', point: 'God knows the details of your life better than you do.' },
];
